# 9. BODY MOVEMENT AND CHAIN OF CUSTODY

This is one of the most important modules.

Every physical movement must create an immutable custody event.

Capture:

- Mortuary case.
- Previous location.
- Destination location.
- Movement type.
- Reason for movement.
- Initiating employee.
- Releasing employee.
- Receiving employee.
- Authorizing employee, where required.
- Date and time.
- Verification method.
- Supporting document or evidence.
- Notes.
- Confirmation signatures.

Movement types may include:

- Initial Reception
- Storage Assignment
- Storage Relocation
- Inspection Movement
- Postmortem Transfer
- External Facility Transfer
- Release Preparation
- Final Handover
- Return to Storage
- Other Authorized Movement

Rules:

- Every movement must have a traceable origin and destination.
- Do not allow an unauthorized employee to approve their own restricted movement where separation of duties is required.
- Require receiving confirmation for custody transfers.
- Support a pending transfer state until the receiving party confirms.
- Prevent duplicate movement submissions.
- Do not permit historical movement records to be edited or deleted.
- Corrections must be recorded as new, linked correction events.

Provide a chronological chain-of-custody timeline on the case details page.

