- Create an incident or maintenance alert when an approved threshold is breached.
- Record corrective action.
- Preserve the full observation history.
- Distinguish manual readings from verified automated readings.

If no real sensor integration exists, implement manual readings and an integration-ready adapter. Do not pretend that live monitoring is available.

# 14. RELEASE AUTHORIZATION AND FINAL HANDOVER

Implement a controlled release workflow.

Before release, validate applicable requirements:

- Correct mortuary case.
- Identity verification status.
- Required documentation.
- Representative identity.
- Representative authority.
- Applicable external clearance.
- Outstanding incident or investigation restrictions.
- Financial clearance, only where hospital policy requires it and subject to lawful exceptions.

Do not automatically block a legally required release based solely on unpaid fees. Financial restrictions must be configurable and reviewed against applicable law and approved hospital policy.

Release statuses:

- Not Requested
- Requested
- Under Review
- Pending Documents
- Pending Authorization
- Approved
- Rejected
- On Hold
- Released

Capture:

- Release applicant.
- Authorized recipient.
- Recipient identity verification.
- Authorization evidence.
- Approving officer.
- Approval date and time.
- Release destination.
- Funeral home or transport provider, if applicable.
- Vehicle or transport details, where required.
- Handover date and time.
- Releasing staff member.
- Receiving person.
- Signatures or approved confirmation.
- Supporting documents.
- Final notes.

Rules:

- A release cannot be finalized without the required approvals.
- A release must be linked to a custody handover event.
- Do not allow a second release for the same active case.
- Do not permit a case to be closed before final handover is confirmed.
- Rejected or cancelled release requests must remain in the audit history.
- Any post-release correction must use an authorized correction workflow.

Generate a printable release and handover report.

